;; clojure-lsp configuration for glitter-uikit.
;;
;; glitter-uikit is a library — its whole point is a public API other projects
;; call, not one this repo calls internally end-to-end. Without this,
;; `clojure-lsp diagnostics` flags every genuinely-public entry point as
;; "unused", which is wrong for a library and makes the linter noisy rather
;; than a useful signal.
;; Classpath discovery must NOT include the :dev alias. clojure-lsp's default
;; for a deps.edn project is `clojure -A:test:dev -Spath`, and this repo's :dev
;; alias exists to override glitter to :local/root "../glitter" — a sibling
;; checkout that exists on a maintainer's machine and nowhere else. On CI that
;; fails with `Local lib io.github.jlt-commons/glitter not found: ../glitter`, and
;; every clojure-lsp gate fails with it, which is exactly what happened on the
;; first green-runner CI run. deps.edn's own :deps pins glitter by :git/sha, so
;; dropping :dev is what makes discovery reproducible off this machine.
{:linters {:clojure-lsp/unused-public-var {:level :off}}
 :project-specs [{:project-path "deps.edn"
                  :classpath-cmd ["clojure" "-A:test" "-Spath"]}]}
